NAME
     init - the first process

SYNOPSIS
     init

DESCRIPTION
     init is process 1. It mounts what /etc/fstab says, runs the scripts
     in /etc/init.d through /etc/rc.d/rc for the runlevel, starts what
     /etc/inittab asks for -- a getty on the console, the daemons -- and
     restarts anything marked respawn when it dies. It reaps orphans,
     and on shutdown it sends TERM, waits, sends KILL, unmounts and
     stops the machine.

     Without an /etc/inittab it starts a shell on the console, which is
     what a guest with a bare root does.

SEE ALSO
     telinit(8), service(8), shutdown(8), inittab(5)
